<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Experiment Configurations</h3>

<section id="A1.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.1.1 </span>Datasets</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Experiments were conducted on data in a 20/80 split (validation/test). See Table <a href="#A1.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ A.1.1 Datasets ‣ A.1 Experiment Configurations ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ HEART: Emotionally-driven test-time scaling of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. For OlympiadBench Physics and Math, the text-only problems were included in our study. Multimodal problems were excluded since the scope of the study is focused on text.</p>
</div>
